    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2401.08383_rag::chunk_008</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2503.05066_rag::chunk_009</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Instead of applying a single FFN to all the input tokens, it first uses a gating function to decide which expert(s) is most suitable for each token</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Token-based routing vs. Expert-based routing</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">systems to route tokens based on token-level semantic similarities</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">N i represents the number of tokens assigned to the i -th expert</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Fetch one sample X , containing a few hundreds of tokens</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the total token allocation satisfying P n i =1 N i = tk</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">each token will be routed by the gating network to top K different experts for processing</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">For each token, a subset of experts is activated to execute computations</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">each tokens tensor data with metadata. By referring to this metadata, the execution engine can select the optimal layer for execution</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Both methods first select experts based on gating scores.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">only a small subset of tokens is typically processed by local experts on a given GPU</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">route each token to a top- k subset of experts</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A learned router computes a distribution over these experts, and assigns input tokens to a small subset.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">select different experts by the router for each token</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">suppose we have N tokens, denoted by T k</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the total proportion of dropped tokens is given by</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">its key concept is to select different experts by the router for each token</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">In each MoE layer, each token will be routed by the gating network to top K different experts for processing</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/S0/R1#enforcesconstrainton">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/S0/R1#expertcapacity"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://example.org/S0/R1#moelayer"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">enforcesConstraintOn</rdfs:label>
    <skos:skos_definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The mechanism by which expert capacity limits the number of tokens processed by MoE layers.</skos:skos_definition>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0049</hasCQ>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0049</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2503.05066_rag::chunk_009</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">expert capacity enforces MoE layers to discard overflowed tokens</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
